{"id": "EUVD-2026-35121", "enisaUuid": "7d085cd6-5c62-3587-ba8f-b49891d60c5a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu/userq: fix access to stale wptr mapping\n\nUse drm_exec to take both locks i.e vm root bo and\nwptr_obj bo to access the mapping data properly.\n\nThis fixes the security issue of unmap the wptr_obj while\na queue creation is in progress and passing other\nbo at same address.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 1fc6c8ab45dbee096469c08c13f6099d57a52d6c)", "datePublished": "2026-06-08T15:50:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T19:36:57", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2da62dbb4169e758c0b1a9378b39a373bf4fb111", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/336a9186f3a4b65bbd865d93936605ac8a1a3991", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6da7b1242da4455b11c24ce667d1cab1a348c8ea"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-46311", "GHSA-9995-3vvw-2xwp"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.1, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a3ddd15-ae27-3bb5-9cae-a9d117049a66", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5fb2f7fc21a3668e5794cc0d153641b9719713e1 <6da7b1242da4455b11c24ce667d1cab1a348c8ea"}, {"id": "29d1283b-be26-35c0-bd22-3486d430425d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.9"}, {"id": "7e65d253-8ef6-3cef-a9a8-d42848e8b4ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5fb2f7fc21a3668e5794cc0d153641b9719713e1 <2da62dbb4169e758c0b1a9378b39a373bf4fb111"}, {"id": "8af26504-2d41-3c6d-87f5-ba52a31d6c59", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "a0bb8707-2c5a-3516-9c2c-7396c16aa9f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16"}, {"id": "c246cd97-6b8d-379d-a23b-a31328cb036f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"nam